Aaj ki class me humne **`matplotlib.pyplot`** (jise standard `import matplotlib.pyplot as plt` ke saath import karte hain) aur Pandas ke **`df.plot()`** ka use karke dataset ko alag-alag tarike se visualize kiya.

Niche saare plotting functions ke detailed notes aur Hinglish comments diye gaye hain:

---

## Matplotlib / Pandas Plotting Cheat Sheet

### 1. Library Import Karna

Visualization start karne ke liye sabse pehle `matplotlib.pyplot` ko import karte hain:

```python
import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

```

---

### 2. Line Plot (Overall Data Trends)

Bina kisi type ke direct `df.plot()` chalane par default Line Plot banta hai.

```python
# Pure DataFrame ko line chart par display karna
df.plot()

# Title aur Axes Label set karna
plt.title("Overall Data Trends")
plt.xlabel("Index / Row Number")
plt.ylabel("Values")

# Graph ko display karna
plt.show()

```

---

### 3. Bar Plot (Categorical vs Numerical Data)

Jab aapko 2 variables (jaise `Age` aur `Salary`) ke values compare karne hon:

```python
# Age ke basis par Salary ka Bar Graph
df.plot(kind='bar', x='Age', y='Salary', color='skyblue', title='Salary by Age')

plt.xlabel('Age')
plt.ylabel('Salary')
plt.show()

```

---

### 4. Histogram (Distribution & Frequency)

Jab kisi single continuous numeric feature (jaise `marks`) ki frequency/range check karni ho:

```python
# Marks ka distribution check karna
df['marks'].plot(kind='hist', bins=5, color='purple', edgecolor='black', title='Marks Distribution')

plt.xlabel('Marks')
plt.ylabel('Frequency')
plt.show()

```

---

### 5. Box Plot (Spread & Outliers)

Data ki min, max, median aur outliers check karne ke liye:

```python
# Specific columns (Age & marks) ka Box Plot
df[['Age', 'marks']].plot(kind='box', title='Age & Marks Box Plot')
plt.show()

```

---

### 6. Scatter Plot (Relationship Between Two Features)

Jab 2 numeric columns ke beech correlation/pattern dekhna ho:

```python
# Marks vs Salary ka Scatter Plot
df.plot(kind='scatter', x='marks', y='Salary', color='red', title='Marks vs Salary Scatter Plot')

plt.xlabel('Marks')
plt.ylabel('Salary')
plt.show()

```

---

### Key Commands Summary:

| Command | Usage (Hinglish) |
| --- | --- |
| `import matplotlib.pyplot as plt` | Plotting module ko `plt` ke short-form name se import karta hai |
| `df.plot(kind='type')` | Chart type define karta hai (`'bar'`, `'hist'`, `'box'`, `'scatter'`) |
| `plt.title("Name")` | Graph ke upar title set karta hai |
| `plt.xlabel() / plt.ylabel()` | X aur Y axis par text-labels lagata hai |
| `plt.show()` | Graph ko Colab screen par clearly render/render karta hai |
